{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "pageVersion": "sha256:9ce95bcf77cbb68169302ee175a58d5ee79433deb67e6c6a5ac059076b9d80f7",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_b1f07316b5d04ea88a57e0690735b343",
      "statement": "The API router separates a public route group requiring no authentication, an API-key-authenticated /webhooks group, a JWT-or-API-key protected group, and a set of public mobile endpoints whose tokens are verified inside the handler rather than by middleware.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/router/api.go#L126-L175",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7bad33074eceb9db8cf8d009f107b580fbff654c2a077d5d4c2842ff7084f8c7:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/router/api.go#L615-L629",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b92c707e5f757afb67891fde78b19d44fee2f8c45c95b9a0a6c37ff3112ed287:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_757c1e0585f1420486479f96be5bb6d7",
      "statement": "The instance public key endpoint is deliberately public because a verifier must obtain the instance public key before it can authenticate anything signed by that instance.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/identity.go#L25-L35",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:75ef2e2a21d221a9d4cd32186a443deb9fdf41c215f49f66b94bb68e897e257d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/router/api.go#L150-L154",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fe197d4f1793dddba49ec3ef6ba3ab6f62f27eb0fa3bed5332e3b494d8d47aa9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3b52821a8ca84c4883c0b5adc3c5275d",
      "statement": "Supabase token validation dispatches on the JWT header algorithm: HS256 uses the configured shared secret as a legacy path, while ES256 and RS256 are verified against public keys fetched from Supabase's JWKS endpoint.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/services/supabase_auth.go#L129-L184",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:107ddea498fd9c205b0bd85a5f907d14b9eb46b07debc3a76fbb769b40421dd8:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/services/supabase_auth.go#L70-L104",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b3e2b54b1ecd48005de730955fccfb3695bf75babe1ff040a3201430ae0139b8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d33c470a787c459083ff87bc5a9c3c82",
      "statement": "JWKS keys are fetched from {SUPABASE_URL}/auth/v1/.well-known/jwks.json, selected by the token's key id, and cached for 10 minutes to match Supabase's documented edge cache TTL, so token verification does not make a network call per request.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/services/supabase_auth.go#L185-L251",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:458e62e37d2903cda8407fa29a34e3183bfc443523e064d241853ec5174797fa:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_52625f5fac70423fb4e8b837039e416e",
      "statement": "SUPABASE_URL is mandatory for the auth middleware, which calls log.Fatal when it is unset, whereas the JWT secret is optional because asymmetric tokens are verified through JWKS.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/supabase_middleware.go#L23-L39",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ea80b6a2f34f8f4cf39d79ce5a9254b3a1b7de96c36832ac372a2214c929c0ea:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7e4eab8a874f4ba89b02c9c46482a37d",
      "statement": "After a Supabase JWT validates, the middleware lazily projects the user into the local users table with provider 'supabase' and a default role of 'engineer' if no record exists, because Supabase owns authentication while the local table is a derived copy.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/supabase_middleware.go#L157-L182",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3dced2292a02bcff48e1ab6807b606e382a3788daa356731e77e867960e2240f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4b1c7ff6310b43a883cc4147bec1de21",
      "statement": "A failure to synchronise the authenticated user into the local database is logged but does not fail the request, so a bookkeeping write error cannot lock out an otherwise valid user.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/supabase_middleware.go#L96-L102",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2c0d17764b36155e21e80db45698780c5ecf70f8fbceea7c7d620b3bf60d328d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cf196ddfb66a4468be2697b8e7a14a0e",
      "statement": "OptionalSupabaseAuth performs the same validation for endpoints that work with or without a user, sets an authenticated flag in context on success, and continues the request chain regardless of the outcome.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/supabase_middleware.go#L114-L148",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:31d666d76f76b3796dfd0fd8dcf185828b175a5800bc5bbfef3f947f78810c6d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_495feb63cf4a4b23bf32cd6509f8c3cd",
      "statement": "API keys are generated as an environment prefix plus 24 hexadecimal characters from crypto/rand, so the target environment is visible in the key itself.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/services/apikey.go#L28-L41",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9339762b0413fe300be852fc8a684800a9c991df257b9253db58767024cb04e3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b61c1808a4004f36b30d75a7503e317c",
      "statement": "API keys are stored bcrypt-hashed and verified with bcrypt.CompareHashAndPassword, so a database disclosure does not yield usable credentials.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/services/apikey.go#L160-L167",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1c65f8157ab07ea10867978ff1ce80d6924788dde33ef966eb614d8430556617:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/services/apikey.go#L43-L50",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d709bb95c76e77600ea2f3398818cf7c24c4faf3ecb628f2169f71822a3f9b65:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_213b899c11e042a4835f9695079231a9",
      "statement": "API key validation additionally rejects keys that are inactive or past their expiry, beyond verifying the hash.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/services/apikey.go#L169-L187",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:694f041cbb31540cad82df95c5304c74d058f786750bafc5ad50830d57d96f98:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6343299f5dcb4ef1879362b5ab806329",
      "statement": "The Supabase auth middleware attempts API key validation on the Authorization header before falling through to JWT validation, and a successful API key sets a synthetic identity plus the key's id, permissions and organization id in request context.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/supabase_middleware.go#L58-L82",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d5fab23f2cd221ce4c2a5727c732072b3680e536bdeabe4cd5b19f0ba6345b2b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2c042fe5482a42ad81e93b8a8ad7dbec",
      "statement": "An API key's last-used timestamp is updated in a background goroutine so the bookkeeping write does not delay the authenticated request.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/supabase_middleware.go#L75-L78",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7b5f97ee7861a5d12f405cebea7e479b41a0012bc301e0e556e97ce0ccf265be:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d12d27f4777d49df846cfdd3a02180ec",
      "statement": "The dedicated webhook API key middleware reads the key from the api_key query parameter rather than a header and enforces per-endpoint permissions, returning 403 when the key lacks them and logging failed authentication attempts.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/apikey.go#L290-L331",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c884c0cf68e2dd59fb4c0e59ffb9c9eeceb1b5f481fd2d3806ffc8c64742a153:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fbf0a44415f94ece819937b4ff3fc00d",
      "statement": "API key rate limiting enforces separate hourly and daily ceilings from the key's own configured limits, but a failure of the rate-limit check itself is logged and the request is allowed to proceed rather than being rejected.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/services/apikey.go#L199-L226",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1d19ee718d02ebdb94c7aadc32691dc5707e301fa829b3349955e30a8c63aef5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_630dff9d3d2443b08b726c70d524568f",
      "statement": "The instance identity is a single ECDSA P-256 keypair resolved database first, then from the data directory file, then generated, with any file-loaded or newly generated key synced back to the instance_identity table so a pod without persistent storage keeps a stable identity across restarts.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/services/identity.go#L145-L215",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d1fdc39f9275683881f348c21d50c52ec491a0de21f3e4f1bbebca6d2b919ba6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/services/identity.go#L60-L98",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6edbbe7434aaa8c28489f01bf1f79feb476e3379aefff26138a29816d7e1231e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2d453c57454e4d7ebd0bb100458a217c",
      "statement": "Instance signatures are SHA-256 hashed and serialised as raw R||S with both halves zero-padded to the curve order size rather than ASN.1 DER, because the raw form is easier for the Web Crypto API to verify.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/services/identity.go#L257-L285",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e839a5aad6616a52d2050ae0086339347e0a12727abf790cf59f3bd2a6e6f11b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f8d656eb12af44a88bc46980310e8cb4",
      "statement": "Signed payloads are canonicalised to JSON with sorted keys before signing, so signer and verifier agree on the exact byte sequence being signed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/services/identity.go#L287-L297",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:002b4160880919aa1217c0e00d65d9bdb357cf0a20056f6309741049e0c042f7:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/services/identity.go#L310-L374",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:328b1c85d9ed39277366f439189d931bf091664bc9df07890540e9bdbffa7905:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_00c2240eef4545f9b725dd5471e54b13",
      "statement": "Device certificate issuance requires an authenticated user, validates the submitted Ed25519 public key length, and signs a payload binding the certificate id, device public key, user id, instance id, permissions and validity window with the instance private key.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/agent.go#L51-L103",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:753e37d24f4fcfd948770485048536e2f6ea5582dbb2dc1e1c92e9b725b0e2d7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c07d44479f264e10a4471310f2f1f519",
      "statement": "Device certificates are issued with a 7-day validity, raised from an earlier 24-hour window for usability.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/agent.go#L80-L84",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b53fece93aa503ed3b3f81d02b629137bf344296872710e4fb3bd0a30297f98f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_af8796b43ebc480e8eb65b951138922f",
      "statement": "The device certificate tracking row is upserted on the (device_id, user_id) pair, so re-enrolling a device replaces its certificate instead of accumulating rows.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/agent.go#L105-L128",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cb9ed857b0f100a0e822b1207975854ba63e15d7067c2285ebb92c806a5b2126:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6131bcb5d09944f5aa34a92007b033d3",
      "statement": "Failure to persist the device certificate tracking row is logged as a warning and the signed certificate is still returned, because the certificate authenticates itself by its instance signature rather than by the database row.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/agent.go#L126-L131",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ffad12eb39ac7cc9e47dfd170560929a3a58e5e62d71c5d50b86a3059a3bbf81:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2f7c58d8c4164d41b179d0899e5200c1",
      "statement": "The trust chain uses two distinct keypairs with distinct scopes: the instance's ECDSA key signs device certificates and never leaves the server, while the device's Ed25519 key signs individual messages and never leaves the device.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/agent/security/verifier.py#L50-L96",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fb83add70a5234c7968e2ad9e41bac61a504621f5e54b4d5236928d8c2821668:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/agent/security/verifier.py#L536-L556",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a16ec2b8bee210d7b9f7e01bad3e42bbf6ef3663111fae1086f25129208e9fa7:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/agent.go#L64-L102",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:433b6f07540f9ff53f8c2ff2b87327f064ab342fe143d5b9d353a70073b69220:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d535ed7740d148f3b6d26fd1a13fa372",
      "statement": "Certificate revocation is scoped to both the certificate id and the requesting user's id so one user cannot revoke another's certificate, and returns 404 when no row matches; listing returns only unrevoked, unexpired certificates.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/agent.go#L151-L200",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e983b2baff5ee37c393ca9014d2513002d118885e7a0b6a9bd635982984ec4e3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_30e3c3a7128044d29525aa100ada725d",
      "statement": "All authentication paths converge on the same request-context keys — user_id, user_email and user_role, plus API-key-specific fields — which is what allows the downstream authorization middleware to behave identically regardless of how the caller authenticated.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/supabase_middleware.go#L104-L112",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:37af5d944f45ca185703128d60ce6602d1af283c6bdb20e5c97dcf904319ab86:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/api/handlers/supabase_middleware.go#L62-L74",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a5fe6687ffcecdad6385a4f16fbdfece0af0364466ccded93b981e28abc6df86:"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
